{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfryZVaBtH7Ur3o4mV1kK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The root cause was mutable default arguments in `inv/warehouse.py`. The fix is in place and both tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** Python evaluates default arguments once, when the function is defined, so every `Warehouse` built without arguments got the same `{}` and `[]` objects:\n\n- `__init__(self, name, stock={}, history=[])`: all warehouses shared one `stock` dict and one `history` list. That is why `b.report()` showed `bolt: 5` from warehouse `a`, and why `restock` on one warehouse changed another.\n- `restock(self, sku, qty, tags=[])`: the same problem for `tags`. A new `Item` received the shared default list, so tags leaked between items.\n\n**Fix** (`inv/warehouse.py`):\n- `__init__` now defaults `stock` and `history` to `None` and creates a fresh `{}` or `[]` per instance. Passing an explicit dict or list still uses that object, so callers who share a store on purpose keep that behavior.\n- `restock` defaults `tags` to `None` and creates `Item(sku, 0, list(tags or []))`. Copying the list also stops a new item from aliasing the caller's list.\n\n**Test:** I did not change `test_independent_warehouses`. I added `test_restock_tags_not_shared` in `tests/test_inv.py` to cover the `tags` case, since the original test did not exercise it.\n\n**Results:**\n- `python -m pytest -q`: 2 passed. Before the fix, `test_independent_warehouses` failed with `{'bolt': 5} == {}`.\n- A quick manual check confirmed `restock`, `ship`, and `report` still work, and that an explicitly passed `stock` dict is used as given.\n\nI did not commit anything. `inv/__init__.py` is empty and was left alone, and nothing else in the repo calls `Warehouse`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12106,"cache_read_input_tokens":28450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12106},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67e77cd2-36ca-4125-8008-2aef010f0b2c","uuid":"2f6bffbe-3ec1-4b3a-956e-4f57a6eb461c","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:26:18.429Z","request_id":"req_011CfryZVJZdvKhwxJfiFhfP"}
